From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0443-starlte-sd-cluster-direct-io.patch - fix to 0436: the
 kernel bounce buffer is for physio's bufs only, not the cluster layer's direct I/O
 (B_PHYS with a UPL, B_CLUSTER), whose buf_map() address is a kernel mapping: the
 bounce's copyout to it failed in copy_validate with EFAULT

S3t/S3u 2026-11-13: every read() through cluster direct I/O on the card root returned EFAULT
after the cached part (the per-user containermanagerd's 6626-byte sandbox profile: 4 KiB,
then EFAULT, 35 starts a boot; no fault line, no copy window: 0442 showed neither). Without
its sandbox containermanagerd exits 0, and Control Center, Finder (pkd), Notification Center
(ChronoServices group container) and the camera service wait on it or crash.
Applies on 0442 (seq-12377 line; starlte_sd.c is 0436's). Kernel seq1n = seq1m + this.
---

--- a/bsd/dev/starlte_sd.c	2026-11-13 13:42:33
+++ b/bsd/dev/starlte_sd.c	2026-11-13 13:42:33
@@ -1761,7 +1761,15 @@
 static inline bool
 sd_buf_is_user(buf_t bp)
 {
-	return (buf_flags(bp) & B_PHYS) && (buf_dataptr(bp) >> 63) == 0;
+	/*
+	 * 0443: only physio's own bufs. The cluster layer's direct I/O (CL_DIRECT_IO: a read
+	 * or write straight into a user buffer, e.g. on an F_NOCACHE file) also sets B_PHYS,
+	 * but carries a UPL (B_CLUSTER) whose b_datap is the UPL offset, a small number:
+	 * buf_map() gives a kernel mapping of the user's pages, and the bounce's copyout to
+	 * that kernel address failed in copy_validate with EFAULT (S3t/S3u 2026-11-13: the
+	 * per-user containermanagerd's read of its sandbox profile, every start).
+	 */
+	return (buf_flags(bp) & (B_PHYS | B_CLUSTER)) == B_PHYS && (buf_dataptr(bp) >> 63) == 0;
 }
 
 static void
